# Keep the container build context small and free of anything local (F05). The Dockerfiles copy only what each image
# needs; this list stops everything else from being sent to the Docker daemon at all.

# Source control metadata (the commit is passed in with --build-arg SOURCE_REVISION instead).
.git
.github

# Build outputs from a local build would otherwise overwrite the clean container build.
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
publish/

# Local data that must never enter an image: GDA-derived models, run results, keys, editor state.
gda-out/
results/
data/uk-full/
# GR-894: the local inbox of reference documents (git-ignored) is not image content.
data/reference-inbox/
**/App_Data/
.vs/
.idea/
*.user

# Licences, keys and local secrets. A licence is mounted at run time (/licence, read-only), never built into an image.
licence/
**/*.gridsim
.env
**/.env
compose.override.yml
token.txt
**/*.token
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.snk

# Large folders the images do not use.
docs/
review-progress/
tests/
tools/

# The exceptions: the files the command line image (Dockerfile.cli) needs from the folders above. The CLI reference
# chapter is compiled into the binary for the per-verb help, and the crossval sidecar ships beside it. An exception
# must come after the folder it reopens.
!docs/manual/0019 CLI reference.md
!tools/crossval/crossval.py
!tools/crossval/sidecar_common.py
